/*
------------------------------------------------------------
Problem    : 3Sum Closest
Platform   : LeetCode
Topic      : Two Pointers
Difficulty : Medium

Problem:
Given an integer array `nums` and an integer `target`,
find three integers whose sum is closest to the target.
Return the sum of those three integers.

Approach:
First, sort the array. Then, fix one element and use the
Two Pointers technique to find the remaining two elements.

For every fixed element, maintain two pointers:
- One starting just after the fixed element.
- One starting from the end of the array.

Calculate the current sum and compare it with the closest
sum found so far. If the current sum is closer to the target,
update the answer. Depending on whether the current sum is
smaller or larger than the target, move the appropriate
pointer to search for a closer sum.

Why does this work?

Sorting the array allows us to efficiently adjust the sum
using two pointers. Moving the left pointer increases the
sum, while moving the right pointer decreases it.

Since every possible triplet is explored in an organized
manner, the algorithm guarantees that the closest sum is
found without checking every combination explicitly.

Algorithm:
1. Sort the array.
2. Initialize the closest sum using the first three elements.
3. Fix one element at a time.
4. Use two pointers to find the best pair.
5. Update the closest sum whenever a better one is found.
6. Move the pointers based on the comparison with the target.
7. Return immediately if an exact match is found.
8. Return the closest sum.

Time Complexity : O(n²)

Reason:
Sorting takes O(n log n), and for each element, the two
pointers traverse the remaining array once.

Space Complexity : O(1)

Reason:
The algorithm uses only constant extra space apart from the
sorting operation.

------------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int threeSumClosest(vector<int>& nums, int target) {

        // Sort the array to apply the Two Pointers technique.
        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        int n = nums.size();

        // Initialize the closest sum.
        int closestSum = nums[0] + nums[1] + nums[2];

        // Fix one element and search for the remaining pair.
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {

            int left = i + 1;
            int right = n - 1;

            while (left < right) {

                int currentSum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];

                // Update the closest sum if a better answer is found.
                if (abs(currentSum - target) < abs(closestSum - target)) {
                    closestSum = currentSum;
                }

                // Increase the sum.
                if (currentSum < target) {
                    left++;
                }

                // Decrease the sum.
                else if (currentSum > target) {
                    right--;
                }

                // Exact target found.
                else {
                    return currentSum;
                }
            }
        }

        return closestSum;
    }
};
